title: 'sc-client-db: do not re-cache header metadata of removed blocks'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    `HeaderMetadataCache` now keeps a bounded list of removed hashes. `BlockchainDb::header_metadata`
    skips caching metadata on a cache miss when the header was removed after it was read, so a header
    removed concurrently by `remove_leaf_block` is never re-cached.
crates:
- name: sc-client-db
  bump: patch
- name: sp-blockchain
  bump: minor
